# Next.js App Router Rules

## Rendering
- **Server Components by default**.
- Use `"use client"` only for state, effects, browser APIs, or client-only libraries.

## Routing & Structure
- Use `app/` routing conventions properly:
  - `app/(site)/...` for public site pages if using route groups
  - `app/blog/...` for blog routes
- Use `layout.tsx` for shared layout, `page.tsx` for routes, `loading.tsx` sparingly.

## Components
- Put reusable UI in `components/`.
- Keep page files thin: orchestrate composition rather than implement heavy UI in `page.tsx`.

## Styling
- Tailwind classes preferred.
- No inline styles unless unavoidable.
- Maintain consistent spacing/typography scale.

## Images & Links
- Use `next/image` for images.
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation.